    <s:String x:Key="HelpExitTitle">Closing and resume</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpExit">When no work is unfinished and Confirm exit is on, the program asks whether to close the window.&#10;&#10;While a download or a transcode is running, the question is asked even if that option is off. It states how many downloads and transcode batches are unfinished. Continue later stores the agreement, and the next launch resumes the work by itself. Don't continue leaves the unfinished work paused and does not ask again on the next launch. Don't exit cancels the close and returns the work to its previous state.&#10;&#10;A pause that was switched on by hand is not included in that count, and the answer does not clear it.&#10;&#10;If the program was stopped abruptly, the next launch offers to continue the interrupted work. Until the question is answered, the old downloads and transcodes do not start. Continue checks finished files on disk first. Not now leaves the interrupted work paused. An interrupted transcode file is encoded from the beginning when the batch continues.</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpSettingsTitle">Settings</s:String>
    <s:String x:Key="HelpSettings">Dark theme and the Color list set the appearance. Save my download preferences stores the choices made in Options.&#10;&#10;Limit the number of simultaneous conversions caps how many files are converted during a download. The new limit applies after a restart. Simultaneous encodes belongs to transcoding of files that are already downloaded, and it applies at once: extra processes stop, and the freed places are taken by the next files. The same value is set in Options and on the Transcode tab.&#10;&#10;At startup the interface language follows the Windows language. A string that has no translation is shown in English. The Language list changes the language until the next launch. YouTube account and Rutube account are described under Sources and accounts.</s:String>
